Keep a shared grid as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared field as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared visited as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared regions as 0.
Place "/\\" into grid.
Place "\\/" into grid.
For every spot from 0 to 35.
Place 0 into field.
Place 0 into visited.

For every row from 0 to 1.
The line is item row of grid.
For every column from 0 to 1.
The piece is the slice of line from column to column plus 1.
The baserow is row times 3.
The basecol is column times 3.
The top is baserow times 6 plus basecol.
If piece matches "/", Set item (top plus 2) of field to 1, Set item (top plus 7) of field to 1, Set item (top plus 12) of field to 1.
If piece matches "\\", Set item top of field to 1, Set item (top plus 7) of field to 1, Set item (top plus 14) of field to 1.

To flood from start (a whole number).
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
Place start into queue.
Set item start of visited to 1.
The head is 0, while the count is 1.
Repeat while head is less than count.
The cell is item head of queue.
Add 1 to head.
The row is cell divided by 6.
The column is cell modulo 6.
If row is more than 0 and item (cell minus 6) of field is 0 and item (cell minus 6) of visited is 0, set item (cell minus 6) of visited to 1, Place (cell minus 6) into queue, add 1 to count.
If row is less than 5 and item (cell plus 6) of field is 0 and item (cell plus 6) of visited is 0, set item (cell plus 6) of visited to 1, Place (cell plus 6) into queue, add 1 to count.
If column is more than 0 and item (cell minus 1) of field is 0 and item (cell minus 1) of visited is 0, set item (cell minus 1) of visited to 1, Place (cell minus 1) into queue, add 1 to count.
If column is less than 5 and item (cell plus 1) of field is 0 and item (cell plus 1) of visited is 0, set item (cell plus 1) of visited to 1, Place (cell plus 1) into queue, add 1 to count.

For every start from 0 to 35.
If item start of field is 0 and item start of visited is 0.
Add 1 to regions.
Flood from start.

Show regions.
